rect CLI command.\\n- The history baseline 6514754a → correction e897db22 → re-measurement db34d3cf, marked as information only.\\n\\nThat report is the author's own account, not an independent adequacy judgment. The conformance obligation now has a realization but still needs semantic assessment.\\n\\nThe rest of the lineage is unchanged and current:\\n- Baseline C2 6514754a is historical evidence about the earlier bytes 647697a5. There, `Hello world!\\\\n` caused 0 passes and 2 failures.\\n- Construction e897db22 made the bounded one-line correction, giving CLI fe8f4080.\\n- C2 db34d3cf on the current CLI: `node generated/hello-world.mjs` exited 0 with exactly `Hello, world!\\\\n`, and `node --test …` exited 0 with 2 passes and 0 failures.\\n\\nThe supplied tests are unchanged, and each spawns the real CLI and asserts status 0 and exact stdout.\\n\\nThree authored assets are still absent: `design/implementation-design.md`, `design/test-design.md` and `test-execution-plan.json`. So the implementation-design, test-design and execution-plan obligations have no realization. Complete-original stays open until those exist and an independent UAT has assessed everything. Behavior and revision already have their realization, verifier-artifact and verifier-execution roles, and each still needs the independent semantic assessment. All seven obligations remain open. The design capability can write all three missing files, and its predecessor authority, the conformance asset, now exists.\",\"contributions\":[{\"graphFunctionRef\":\"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/design@5\",\"contribution\":\"Write only these three files. Treat the current `specification/project-conformance.md` (sha256:9d02e5fb…) as authority, and trace to its R-/AC- identifiers where applicable.\\n\\n1. `design/implementation-design.md`\\n- Uses the conformance asset as authority.\\n- Defines the minimal Node CLI at `generated/hello-world.mjs`. The actual current surface is `console.log(\\\"Hello, world!\\\");`, which prints exactly `Hello, world!` followed by one newline, exits 0 and needs no package installation or network.\\n- Names the component and UAT test source surfaces, `test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs` and `test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs`. Both run `spawnSync(process.execPath, ['generated/hello-world.mjs'], { encoding: 'utf8' })` from the project root and assert status and stdout.\\n- Keeps the conformance conflicts and unknowns visible, including C-1: execution-result meaning is carried by admitted C2 evidence, not by an authored receipt.\\n\\n2. `design/test-design.md`\\n- Specifies component and UAT validation of the CLI stdout contract, matching the actual supplied tests.\\n- Both tests use `node:test`, `node:assert/strict` and `node:child_process` `spawnSync`.\\n- Both spawn `node generated/hello-world.mjs` from the project root and assert status 0 and stdout exactly `Hello, world!\\\\n`.\\n- The pass criterion under `node --test` is at least 2 passes and `fail 0`, with at least one pass from each test file.\\n- Records that the baseline failure (6514754a, on earlier bytes) showed these verifiers detect the missing comma.\\n\\n3. `test-execution-plan.json`\\n- `command`: `\\\"node\\\"`\\n- `args`: `[\\\"--test\\\",\\\"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs\\\",\\\"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs\\\"]`\\n- `expectedTestPassCount`: at least 2\\n- `expectedStdoutMatch`: stable zero-failure evidence such as `fail 0`, with no exact pass-count fragment\\n- `assertedReturnValue`: `\\\"Hello, world!\\\"`\\n- Resolve U-5 explicitly. The plan may add a separate entry for the direct CLI check `node generated/hello-world.mjs`, expecting exit 0 and stdout `Hello, world!\\\\n`, as long as the required top-level fields stay exactly as above.\\n- The plan is prospective. It must agree with the two fixed commands, does not control execution, and must not embed fabricated observed results.\\n\\nWrite no `test-execution-result.json`. Do not modify the CLI, tests,